WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:17.015
Nearby, down the side of the hill, some gravel fell and rattled through the trees.

2
00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:24.642
My eyes turned instinctively in that direction, and I saw a dark figure quickly leap behind the trunk of a large tree.

3
00:00:24.643 --> 00:00:30.362
I couldn't tell if it was a bear or a monkey, but it seemed large and shaggy.

4
00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:37.918
I was cut off on both sides; behind me were murderers, and in front of me was this lurking animal.

5
00:00:37.919 --> 00:00:46.896
Suddenly, Long John seemed the lesser of two evils, so I turned and, looking over my shoulder, started heading back toward the boats.

6
00:00:46.897 --> 00:00:54.349
Instantly, the figure swiftly moved through the trees, running manlike on two legs yet hunched over.

7
00:00:54.350 --> 00:01:01.028
This creature was unlike any man I'd ever seen, but it was a man.

8
00:01:01.029 --> 00:01:07.276
"Maybe it's a cannibal," I said to myself, and I almost called out to the pirates for help.

9
00:01:07.277 --> 00:01:11.778
But the mere fact he was a man, however wild, reassured me.

10
00:01:11.779 --> 00:01:16.275
"Wait, I have a pistol," I thought. "I'm not defenseless!"

11
00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:24.097
So I walked toward the island man, and as soon as I moved in his direction, he stepped toward me.

12
00:01:24.098 --> 00:01:32.950
He hesitated, but at last, to my wonder and confusion, he threw himself on his knees and held out his clasped hands.

13
00:01:32.951 --> 00:01:35.810
"Who are you?" I asked.

14
00:01:35.811 --> 00:01:41.972
"I'm poor Ben Gunn," he said in a voice that was hoarse, like a rusty lock.

15
00:01:41.973 --> 00:01:47.574
"I haven't spoken with a soul for three years."

16
00:01:47.575 --> 00:01:54.897
His skin was all sunburned, his lips were black, and his fair eyes looked bright in his dark face.

17
00:01:54.898 --> 00:02:03.766
His clothing was a tattered ship's canvas and ragged, old cloth fastened together with small sticks and loops of animal hide.

18
00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:06.496
"Were you shipwrecked?" I cried.

19
00:02:06.497 --> 00:02:11.874
"No, mate," he said, "marooned."

20
00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:13.835
I knew what that meant.

21
00:02:13.836 --> 00:02:23.505
Being marooned was a horrible punishment in which a pirate was left behind on a desolate island, with only a little gunpowder and one bullet.

22
00:02:23.506 --> 00:02:35.743
"Marooned three years ago," Gunn went on. "I've lived on goats, berries, and oysters. But my heart craves a civilized diet.

23
00:02:35.744 --> 00:02:46.754
You don't happen to have a piece of cheese? No? Well, many long nights I've dreamed of cheese—toasted, mostly."

24
00:02:46.755 --> 00:02:52.055
"If I ever get aboard again," I said, "you shall have plenty of cheese."

25
00:02:52.056 --> 00:03:01.411
As we talked, he was feeling my jacket, smoothing my hands, and generally showing a childish pleasure in the presence of a fellow creature.

26
00:03:01.412 --> 00:03:04.204
"I'm Jim," I said.

27
00:03:04.205 --> 00:03:15.441
"Jim, Jim," he repeated, quite pleased. "Well, now, Jim, can you believe I once had a devoted mother who looked after me?"

28
00:03:15.442 --> 00:03:18.892
"Not really," I answered.

29
00:03:18.893 --> 00:03:23.774
"I was a polite, churchgoing boy too," Gunn said.

30
00:03:23.775 --> 00:03:29.323
"I've thought about it here on this lonely island, and I've decided to go back to church someday.

31
00:03:29.324 --> 00:03:39.139
I'll be good again. I know how. And Jim"—looking all around him and lowering his voice to a whisper—"I'm rich."

32
00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:42.369
This poor fellow was crazy, I thought.

33
00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:50.377
I must have looked unconvinced, for he repeated, "Rich! Rich! And I'll make you rich too, Jim.

34
00:03:50.378 --> 00:03:53.368
You'll be thankful you found me first!"

35
00:03:53.369 --> 00:04:01.242
Suddenly a shadow came over his face, and Gunn grabbed my arm and raised a forefinger threateningly at me.

36
00:04:01.243 --> 00:04:06.901
"Tell the truth—is that Flint's ship?" he asked.

37
00:04:06.902 --> 00:04:12.878
Right then, I knew I'd found an ally. "It's not Flint's ship! Flint is dead.

38
00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:17.763
But some of Flint's men are aboard, which is bad luck for the rest of us."

39
00:04:17.764 --> 00:04:22.574
"Is there a man . . . with one leg?" he gasped.

40
00:04:22.575 --> 00:04:25.483
"He's the cook and the ringleader."

41
00:04:25.484 --> 00:04:30.715
Gunn was still holding me by the wrist, and he squeezed hard.

42
00:04:30.716 --> 00:04:36.884
"If you were sent by Long John Silver," he whispered, "I'm as good as dead."

43
00:04:36.885 --> 00:04:43.904
I told him the whole story of our voyage and predicament, and when I was done, he patted me on the head.

44
00:04:43.905 --> 00:04:50.204
"You're a good lad, Jim," said Gunn. "You're all in a bad situation.

45
00:04:50.205 --> 00:04:56.945
Well, put your trust in me. Would your squire share Flint's treasure and give me passage home?"

46
00:04:56.946 --> 00:05:05.872
"Yes," I cried. "We all planned to share, and besides, without the pirates, we'll need you to help sail the vessel home."

47
00:05:05.873 --> 00:05:11.422
"Ah," said he, "so you would." And he seemed relieved.

48
00:05:11.423 --> 00:05:18.074
"I was on Flint's ship," he continued, "when he and six men buried the treasure.

49
00:05:18.075 --> 00:05:23.092
The rest of us waited on the old Walrus until Flint returned, alone.

50
00:05:23.093 --> 00:05:26.277
It must have been quite a battle, six against one.

51
00:05:26.278 --> 00:05:31.781
Billy Bones was the first mate, and Long John was quartermaster.

52
00:05:31.782 --> 00:05:37.930
The men on board asked Flint where the treasure was, and he said, 'Go ashore, if you like, and stay there—

53
00:05:37.931 --> 00:05:43.359
but as for the ship, she'll hunt for more, by thunder!' That's what he said."

54
00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.489
"How were you marooned?" I asked.

55
00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:52.044
"Well, a few years later, I was on another ship and we sighted this island.

56
00:05:52.045 --> 00:05:57.937
'Boys,' I said, 'Flint's treasure is here. Let's find it.'

57
00:05:57.938 --> 00:06:05.134
For 12 days, we looked but didn't find the treasure, and with each passing day, they got angrier at me.

58
00:06:05.135 --> 00:06:10.278
One morning, they just said, 'Here's a musket, spade, and pickax.

59
00:06:10.279 --> 00:06:15.170
Find Flint's money yourself.' And the ship set sail without me.

60
00:06:15.171 --> 00:06:22.878
So, Jim, I've been here three years, and I haven't had a bite of decent food since."

61
00:06:22.879 --> 00:06:28.373
"We need to get back on board the Hispaniola," I said. "But how?"

62
00:06:28.374 --> 00:06:31.972
"I have a small boat I made," answered Gunn.

63
00:06:31.973 --> 00:06:36.931
"I keep her under the white rock. We can try to get to the ship after dark."

64
00:06:36.932 --> 00:06:43.029
Suddenly the island echoed with cannon thunder, and Gunn and I ran toward the anchorage.

65
00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:49.119
We heard gunshots ring out next, and then, not a quarter of a mile away was a startling sight.

66
00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:58.473
Fluttering above the woods was our country's flag, the Union Jack.
